Now pull in the full program and match it against what you know. Look for what's genuinely a strong fit, not just what's popular — an artist that fits their taste even if they've never heard of them, a talk by someone worth meeting, an exhibit that lines up with something they mentioned caring about. Look into what each candidate is actually about; don't just match on titles or keywords.

Don't print a formatted list here — that comes at the end. Instead, surface your strongest find first ("this looks like a clear win for you, because...") and confirm it lands before building out the rest around it. Keep going conversationally, one or a few finds at a time, until you both have a shortlist that feels solid. When you're there, call advance_flow with a short note of what made the cut and why.
